<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-QTC sees 97/98 borrowings A$2.494 billion.</title>
<headline>RTRS-QTC sees 97/98 borrowings A$2.494 billion.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Queensland Treasury Corp, the borrowing agency of the state of Queensland, said on Wednesday it estimated its gross borrowing requirement for 1997/98 to June 30 at A$2.494 billion, compared with actual raisings of A$5.565 billion in 1996/97.</p>
<p>The 1996/97 raisings compare with an initial estimate for borrowings of A$4.150 billion.</p>
<p>QTC said it expected to issue A$80 million to A$120 million of domestic bonds on a tap basis each month, although actual financial market activity and actual funding requirements may vary depending on client requirements and market conditions.  </p>
<p>Net of Samurai and short dated QTC bond redemptions, gross borrowings totalled about A$4.55 billion in 1996/97.</p>
<p>A QTC spokesman said the difference between estimated and actual raisings for 1996/97 mainly reflected early redemptions.</p>
